=== PARITY (vs web NotFoundPage.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> the web source has NO data hook (the manifest declares none): it renders from
    navigation values / local state. `useTranslation` + a synchronous `useMemo(closestRoutes(…))`.
    The native parity binds through a local P1/S8 state holder (NotFoundPageModel) that owns
    `unmatchedPath` and DERIVES the closest-route suggestions on read (the @Observable analogue of
    the web useMemo). The view performs no HTTP — there is none to perform.
  Engine -> NotFoundText.normalize + levenshtein are faithful ports of web closestRoute.ts
    (lower-case + strip [\s\-_/], iterative two-row Levenshtein). NotFoundSuggestionEngine.closest
    ports closestRoutes: rank each registry entry by min(distance(path), distance(identifier)),
    keep distance <= 6, sort by distance then path, take 5. The web ROUTE_REGISTRY (browser routes,
    excluding parameterized/hidden) maps to AppRoute.allCases — every native route is directly
    navigable, so a tapped suggestion sets a real shell selection (web <Link to={path}>).
    Verified by executed XCTest (kitten/sitting=3, vehiclees/vehicles=1, baterry/battery=2;
    "/vehiclees" -> .vehicles first @ distance 1; far query -> []; blank -> []; sorted ascending).
  Composition -> one centered glass panel (web GlassPanel `mx-auto max-w-2xl`, "GlassPanel1") with:
    compass header (web lucide Compass -> SF `safari`, decorative) over the heading + the break-all
    body line; the "Did you mean" suggestion list (web <ul>/<Link>, hidden when none = web
    `suggestions.length > 0 &&`); and the back / dashboard / command-palette action row (web Button
    row, ArrowLeft/Home/Search -> SF arrow.left/house/magnifyingglass), adaptive H<->V via ViewThatFits.
  Shared components -> TSGlassPanel (web GlassPanel), TSButton (web Button), the design tokens
    (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius). Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (no chart/map).
  States (all render) -> the manifest declares ONE data state: `success`. There is no async data
    source, so the generic loading / empty / error / stale / offline states have NO trigger on this
    surface (web parity = matching the source; reproducing them would fabricate behavior absent from
    the spec, Honesty rule 3). The page ALWAYS renders content (never a blank region): the only
    conditional is the suggestion block, which collapses to just the header + actions when there are
    no close matches — exactly the web `suggestions.length > 0 && …`.
  i18n -> all 7 source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade (NotFoundStrings, default catalog) with
    the web `t(key, default)` fallback, verbatim web defaults: notFound.title ("Page not found"),
    notFound.heading ("We couldn't find that page"), notFound.body ("%@ doesn't match any route." =
    web "{{path}} doesn't match any route." with the path interpolated), notFound.didYouMean
    ("Did you mean:"), notFound.goBack ("Go back"), notFound.goHome ("Go to dashboard"),
    notFound.openSearch ("Open command palette"). No English literals in native code.
  a11y -> the compass glyph is decorative (.accessibilityHidden); the heading+body combine into one
    element; each suggestion is an `.isLink` element with a label (route title) + hint (path); the
    action icons are decorative (text label conveys meaning); the page exposes a combined VoiceOver
    summary (NotFoundAccessibility.summary). Dynamic Type via tokens; targets >= 28-44pt. Light/dark
    + increased-contrast honored through the dynamic Color.TS tokens (ADR-015).
  Telemetry -> NotFoundPageModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"NotFoundPage") AND notFound(path:)
    exactly once (the web `useEffect(() => console.warn('[404]', path))`) via the P1/S11 seam.
    Asserted by a spy test (fires once across two start() calls; slug == "NotFoundPage").
  Navigation -> NotFoundDeepLink.resolve(path:) is the native <Route path="*"> fallthrough: a known
    path (incl. web aliases like "/" -> dashboard, "/battery" -> energy via AppRouteParser) yields
    `.route`, anything else yields `.notFound(path:)`; NotFoundRouteRegistration.page mounts the page
    with the shell's back/home/palette/navigate actions. The page sets its navigationTitle from
    notFound.title (web usePageTitle). Unit-tested (known/alias/unmatched).

